From 67a6d59fffcab584f0a93b759fef25de8b7f2db1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 17:40:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(gateway): content preview + main-turn ACK for busy
 session UX
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem
-------
Two remaining UX gaps after queue-mode ACK v1:

  * "📥 Queued #1" told the user their message was in position 1, but
    nothing about WHICH message. When multiple follow-ups queue during a
    busy turn and responses come back out of visible order, users could
    not map replies to inputs.
  * A message arriving on an idle session (first turn in the window)
    started the agent immediately with zero visible receipt. On slow
    turns the user waited in silence with no confirmation the message
    was even seen.

Fix
---
Two changes, both reuse the shared 30s ``_busy_ack_ts`` debounce so the
whole "one ACK per session per window" invariant still holds.

1. **Content preview in queue ACK.** New helper
   ``_msg_preview_for_ack(event, max_chars=25)`` returns a quoted,
   whitespace-normalised, truncated snippet of the inbound text (or a
   ``[voice]`` / ``[photo]`` placeholder for media). Queue ACK format
   changes from ``📥 Queued #{N} (排队中)`` to
   ``📥 排队 #{N}: "preview..." (Queued)``.

2. **Main-turn ACK.** New helper ``_maybe_send_main_turn_ack`` fires
   from ``_handle_message`` just before ``_handle_message_with_agent``
   when a message starts the main turn (session was idle). Same master
   ``HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_ACK_ENABLED`` gate. New per-mode toggle
   ``HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_MAIN_ACK_ENABLED`` /
   ``display.platforms.<platform>.busy_main_ack_enabled`` (default true)
   lets platforms opt out separately from queue/steer/interrupt ACKs.
   Skipped for internal events (background-process completions,
   goal-continuations) so system-driven turns stay silent.

   Format: ``⏳ 处理中: "preview..." (Working)``.

Numbering semantics: main-turn ACK has no position number (it is the
"current" turn by definition). Queue ACK numbers are 1-indexed
positions in the FIFO queue behind the current turn — ``#1`` = "next up
after main", ``#2`` = "after that", etc.

Tests
-----
Updated tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py:
  * test_busy_text_mode_queue_sends_ack_by_default now asserts the new
    format (排队 #N + preview substring).
  * New TestMainTurnAck class (5 tests) covers: sent by default,
    debounced within window, opt-out via env, skipped for internal
    events, master switch off.

Full suite: 55/55 pass.

Backlog ref: agents/todo/backlog/2026-07-20_020_...ack-ux.md
